@@ -241,6 +242,32 @@ end sees stage 0 and the diffuse colour), so effects that need a second stage
 or a combiner program only appear on the CPU rasteriser. Extend `Nv2aBatch`
 when it matters rather than adding callbacks.
 
+## Bounded GPU audit
+
+`RECOMP_GPU_AUDIT=1` writes cumulative CSV diagnostics to
+`RECOMP_GPU_AUDIT_FILE` (default `gpu_audit.csv`). `batch_geometry` correlates
+primitive, input source, route and output scope. `post_clip_triangles` counts
+CPU-transformed triangles emitted after clipping; GPU-vertex submissions are
+pre-clip and do not supply a post-clip count. Neither emitted nor submitted
+geometry proves that any pixel was visible. The older `output` count mixes
+these scopes and must not be interpreted as a visibility measurement.
+
+For unsupported primitives, `unsupported_state` combines the primitive with
+a bitset: bits 0–1 transform mode, 2 composite matrix set, 3 any colour write,
+4 depth test, 5 depth write, 6 stencil test, 7 blend, 8 alpha test, 9 window
+clip, and 10 zeta bound; `unsupported_size` reports the target dimensions.
+`recent_method_for_drop` associates a dropped request with at most eight
+recent unhandled or mirror-only methods, expiring after 256 method events or
+a flip. These are temporal clues, not proven causes.
+
+`cpu_depth_binding` records request-time CPU bindings of formats `0x2E` and
+`0x41`, including exact equality with the current zeta address; it does not
+prove that a texture was sampled. The CPU sampler does not decode `0x2E`,
+while `0x41` samples guest bytes; CPU depth uses a separate float buffer and
+stencil is not modeled there. Frame traces label transformed input vertices as
+pre-clip and never reuse a prior CPU vertex buffer for a GPU-vertex submission.
+All audit tables have bounded capacity and report overflow.
+
 ## Switches
 
 | Variable | Does |
